Jonathan Prag</div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\"><div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><a id=\"al1-diplomatic\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"ἐνθάδε\">[......</span><span data-text=\"κῖτε\">....</span><span data-text=\"ἡ\">.</span><span data-text=\"μακαρία\">.......]</span><br id=\"al2-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Ἄπρα\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἄπρα\">ΑΠΡΑ</span></span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Κεντιανοῦ θυγάτηρ\n                    καὶ Ἀσκληπιαδότης\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"patronym\" data-text=\"Κεντιανοῦ\">[..]ΝΤΙΑΝΟΥ</span><span data-text=\"θυγάτηρ\">ΘΥΓΑΤΗΡ</span><br id=\"al3-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span><span data-text=\"καὶ\">ΚΑΙ</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Ἀσκληπιαδότης\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"matronym\" data-text=\"Ἀσκληπιαδότης\">ΑΣΚΛΗΠΙΑΔΟΤ[..</span></span></span><span data-text=\"δούλη\">.....]</span><br id=\"al4-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Χριστοῦ\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Χριστοῦ\"><span class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">Χ</span><span class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">Υ</span></span></span><span data-text=\"ἀγαθή\">ΑΓΑΘΗ</span><span data-text=\"δένδρον\">ΔΕΝΔΡΟ[.</span><span data-text=\"καλῶς\">.....]</span><br id=\"al5-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span><span data-text=\"ἐν\">ΕΝ</span><span data-text=\"πίστι\">ΠΙΣΤΙ</span><span data-text=\"ἐφυτευμένον\">ΕΦΥΤΕΥΜ[....]</span><br id=\"al6-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">6</span><span data-text=\"τῇ\">ΤΗ</span><span data-text=\"ὀλυγοχρονίᾳ\">ΟΛΥΓΟΧΡΟΝΙΑ</span><span data-text=\"ἀποχω\n                    ριθῖσα\">[.....]<br id=\"al7-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">7</span>ΡΙΘΙΣΑ</span><span data-text=\"καὶ\">ΚΑΙ</span><span data-text=\"τῆς\">ΤΗΣ</span><span data-text=\"τοῦ\">ΤΟΥ</span><span data-text=\"κόσμου\">[......]</span><br id=\"al8-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">8</span><span data-text=\"ἀγάπης\">ΑΓΑΠΗΣ</span><span data-text=\"λύπην\">ΛΥΠΗΝ</span><span data-text=\"καταλιποῦ\n                    σα\">ΚΑΤ[......]<br id=\"al9-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">9</span>ΣΑ</span><span data-text=\"τοῖς\">ΤΟΙΣ</span><span data-text=\"ἰδίοις\">ΙΔΙΟΙΣ</span><span data-text=\"Ἐπλήρωσε\">ΕΠΛΗΡ[...</span><span data-text=\"τὸ\">..]</span><br id=\"al10-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">10</span><span data-text=\"τῆς\">ΤΗΣ</span><span data-text=\"ψυχῆς\">ΨΥΧΗΣ</span><span data-text=\"δάνος\">ΔΑΝΟΣ</span><span data-text=\"τελευτῶσα\">ΤΕΛΕ[.....]</span><br id=\"al11-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">11</span><span data-text=\"καλένδαις\">ΚΑΛ</span><span data-text=\"Ἀπριλίων\">ΑΠΡΙΛΙΩΝ</span>ΥΠΑΤ[..<span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Θεοδο\n                    σίου\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Θεοδο\n                    σίου\">.....]<br id=\"al12-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">12</span>ΣΙΟΥ</span></span><span data-text=\"τὸ\">ΤΟ</span>ΕΙ<span data-text=\"καὶ\">Κ</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Βαλεντινιάνου\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Βαλεντινιάνου\">ΒΑΛΕΝΤΙΝΙΑ[...</span></span><span data-text=\"τὸ\">..]</span><br id=\"al13-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">13</span>Δ</span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div></div>  <div id=\"facsimile-images\"><h2>Facsimile Images</h2></div>  <div id=\"apparatus\"><h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span><span>Text of Agnello</span></span>; </li><li><span class=\"line 1\">line.1: <span>ἐντάδε sic AE 1933.25</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 8\">line.8: <span>ΛΥΓΗΣ sic AE 1933.25</span></span></li></ul></div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo</a></p>  <p>Here lies the blessed Apra, daughter of Kentianos and Asklepiodote, a good servant of Christ, a tree well planted in the faith, torn away from her brief life and from the affections of this world, leaving sorrow to her own. She returned the loan of her soul, dying on the Kalends of April during the fifteenth consulship of Theodosius and the fourth consulship of Valentinian.</p>  </div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2>Italian translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\">  </p><p>Qui giace la beata Apra, figlia di Quinziano e di Asclepiodote, bouna serva di Cristo, albero ben piantato nella fede, dipartitasi dalla vita terrena e dagli affetti del mondo, lasciando dolore tra i suoi. Restitui il prestito della vita morendo il 1 aprile sotto il quindicesimo consolato di Teodosio ed il quarto di Valentiniano [trad. di Agnello]</p>  </div>  <div id=\"commentary\"><h2>commentary</h2>  <p>The epitaph commemorates the young deceased Apra, daughter of Kentianos and Asklepiodote. For the name Apra, which may represent a variant of Apronia or Aphronia. The father's name is partially restored by Libertini (1931, 40), who also proposed alternative readings, including Sentianus, Gentianus, Ventianus, and Mintianus. The deceased is described as <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">δούλη Χ(ριστο)ῦ ἀγαθή</span> (ll. 3–4; cf. IG XIV 442 = <a href=\"https://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic001267\" target=\"_blank\">ISic001267</a>) and, through a poetic image, as <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">δένδρο[ν καλῶς] | ἐν πίστει ἐφυτευμ[ένον</span> (ll. 4–5), an expression that echoes a well-established image in Christian theology (cf. [Athan.] 28.712.45). The brevity of her life is conveyed by the expression <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">τῇ ὀλιγοχρονίᾳ</span> (l. 6) and by the reference to <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">τοῖς ἰδίοις</span> (l. 9), from whose affection she was torn away. The mention of her parents, together with the absence of any reference to a husband, led Libertini (1931, 41) to suggest that she died a virgin. At l. 10, the expression <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">τῆς ψυχῆς δάνος</span> refers to the soul as a loan that is returned to God after death. Finally, ll. 10–13 conclude the epitaph with the date of the deceased's death, which occurred on the Kalends of April during the fifteenth consulship of Theodosius and the fourth consulship of Valentinian. This internal dating places the inscription in AD 435.</p>  </div>  <div id=\"bibliography\"><h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Libertini 1931 40 n.1 tav. A.1 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001870\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001870</a></li><li> 1933 25 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001283\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001283</a></li><li> Agnello 1953 no.96 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002211\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002211</a></li></ul>  <ul><li></li></ul>  </div>  <div id=\"handnote\"> Line 1-13  15  Interlineation line 1 to 2    </div><div id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. </div>",
